no-trailing-spaces (MD009), Whitespace and layout
On by default, severity warning. Fixable.
Your configuration sets its severity to error.

Outside code blocks, lines end in no spaces or tabs, or in exactly 2 of them.

Why: Trailing whitespace in text does not change the output, except where 2 or
more spaces make a hard line break. In code blocks it is part of the code.

Tags: whitespace

Options, under rules.no-trailing-spaces.options:
  br_spaces (integer, default 2)
    Trailing spaces allowed for a hard line break. Values below 2 allow none.
  list_item_empty_lines (boolean, default false)
    Allow trailing spaces on empty lines inside list items.
  strict (boolean, default false)
    Also report br_spaces where they make no line break, such as at the end of a
    paragraph.
  ignore_code_blocks (boolean, default true)
    Skip the lines of code blocks. Also accepted as code_blocks, with the
    opposite value.

Fix: The fix deletes the trailing whitespace, or trims a hard line break to
exactly 2 spaces. gomdlint reports some trailing whitespace without a fix, such
as whitespace inside a code span, which is code, or a tab where the paragraph
goes on to the next line, which some renderers read as a hard line break.
gomdlint may report a finding without a fix when the fix would change a line
with one character in brackets, such as [x] or [1], or the lines around it up to
a blank line, because it could add or remove a task list checkbox. In a document
with raw HTML other than comments and plain br, wbr, hr or img tags, gomdlint
reports every finding without a fix.

This document breaks the rule:
  | # Guide
  |
  | Install the tool. 
  | Then run it in the project root.

gomdlint reports:
  3:18 Trailing whitespace

The fix changes it to:
  | # Guide
  |
  | Install the tool.
  | Then run it in the project root.

Configure:
  rules:
    no-trailing-spaces:
      options:
        br_spaces: 2

Under rules, no-trailing-spaces: false turns the rule off and
no-trailing-spaces: error reports its findings as errors. The flag
--disable no-trailing-spaces turns it off for one run.

Silence one line:
  <!-- markdownlint-disable-next-line no-trailing-spaces -->

markdownlint: https://github.com/DavidAnson/markdownlint/blob/v0.41.1/doc/md009.md
